app.withGlobalTauri is on, so the site can call the three commands without a bundler. They
exist only in the desktop tier; check detectTier() === 'desktop' (or window.TAURI)
first.

// Opens the native folder picker. Resolves to the canonical absolute path the user picked
// (a string; use it as config.data.path) or null if they cancelled. Rejects with a message
// string if the folder cannot be granted.
const folder = await window.TAURI.core.invoke('pick_data_folder');

// Opens the native file picker for a GGUF model. Resolves to the canonical path of the chosen
// file (now readable by the backend, that file only) or null if cancelled. Rejects with a
// message string if it is not a .gguf file with the GGUF magic bytes.
const gguf = await window.TAURI.core.invoke('pick_gguf_file');

// Resolves to {phase, message, progress, line, error, port, accelerator, torchIndex, python, logDir,
//              ollama: {reachable, url, version, error} | null}
// phase: "setup" | "starting" | "ready" | "error"
const status = await window.TAURI.core.invoke('backend_status');

* one conversation: delete it in the app (asks) or remove jev-data/workspaces/<id>/;
* everything at once from the app: JEV > Settings > Your data > Delete all data (asks; keeps
  settings.json and, if you tick it, the audit log). Export all data first gives you a zip of
  every conversation, file and audit row;
* all of JEV's data including settings: delete the jev-data/ folder;
* models: jev models rm NAME / ollama rm NAME, or delete Ollama's models folder;
* JEV itself: pip uninstall jepa-studio.

1. pip install -e ".[dev]", then python -m pytest -q tests/test_jev_sandbox.py tests/test_jev_tools.py tests/test_media_ffmpeg.py:
   all must pass with jev doctor reporting method sandbox-exec.
2. In jev chat, approve run_python with each of these and check every one fails:
   import socket; socket.create_connection(("1.1.1.1", 80));
   open(os.path.expanduser("~/Desktop/x"), "w"); open(os.path.expanduser("~/.ssh/id_rsa")).read();
   reading jev-data/settings.json; os.system("open -a Calculator");
   subprocess.run(["osascript", "-e", "display dialog \"x\""]); subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/pbpaste"]).
3. Check that numpy, matplotlib and torch import and run, and that run_node works.
4. Only then set MACOS_PROFILE_VERIFIED = True (and note the macOS version in the commit).

